{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>They journeyed from here</b> — they moved themselves from the Ahvah. \"Let us go to Dothan\" — to seek for you devices of death by which they would kill you. And according to its plain sense it is a place-name, and a verse does not depart from its plain sense — the language of R. Solomon. And the intent of our Sages is not that the man explained to him, \"They journeyed from here,\" as meaning from the Ahvah, \"and went to stir up against you judgments and accusations,\" for if so he would have refrained from going and would not have endangered himself. Rather, their intent is that the man was Gabriel, and what he told him he told truly, and he spoke language that serves two meanings, and both are true, but he did not understand what was hidden in it and went after what was revealed to him: \"and he went after his brothers and found them in Dothan,\" as he had told him. And they expounded this because this man is an angel, and if so he knows where they are; and why did he not say, \"Here they are in Dothan,\" but rather spoke as though in doubt — as if he had heard from them that they would go there but does not know where they are now? Therefore they make a midrashic exposition of his statement:" "<b>For I heard them saying</b> — I heard them, who were saying, \"Let us go to Dothan.\" And likewise, \"and Rebekah was listening\" (Genesis 27:5) — she was listening. And it is possible that he means: \"The shepherds journeyed from here, for I heard men saying, 'Let us go to Dothan' — perhaps they are your brothers.\" He spoke with him as one concealing his face from the matter:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {0 "I have rendered אַחְוָה as \"the Ahvah\" (the place name at Genesis 37:14, Shechem's grazing land) since Ramban here treats it as a specific location.", 1 "The phrase מַסְתִּיר פָּנִים is rendered literally as 'concealing his face from the matter'; the idiom suggests the man spoke as though distancing himself from knowledge of the affair."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:07.187803098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}